Hi,

 

I found something weird in my aov output.

 

I am running an repeated measure anova analysis in R using the aov function (the reason I did this was because my LME model did not converge).

 

So in two psychophysical experiments, participants saw a line presented for a certain duration; they later either reproduced the length or duration of the line. So here, I have Length and Duration as within-subject participant factors, and Exp as the between-subject factor (data attached).

 

E12L <- read.table ("E12L.txt", TRUE)

E12L$Subject = factor (E12L$Subject)

E12L$cDuration = scale(E12L$Duration,center = TRUE, scale = FALSE)

E12L$cLength = scale(E12L$Length,center = TRUE, scale = FALSE)

E12L$cExp = scale(E12L$Exp,center = TRUE, scale = FALSE)

e12l=lmer(LengthR~cExp*cDuration+cLength+(cDuration+cLength+1|Subject),E12L)

summary(e12l) ***DOES NOT CONVERGE****

e12l.aov = aov (LengthR~(cExp+cDuration+cLength)+Error(Subject/(cDuration+cLength)),E12L)

summary(e12l.aov)

 

