On Jul 7, 2015, at 10:40 AM, Dale Barr <dale.barr-Rvdaw4MAOY42EctHIo1CcQ at public.gmane.org<mailto:dale.barr-Rvdaw4MAOY42EctHIo1CcQ at public.gmane.org>> wrote:

Zhenguang,

With 1400+ observations on 59 units, you really should have enough data to estimate all seven random effects parameters.  However, your predictors are all on very different scales. You have:

Exp:      [1, 2]
Duration: [1000, 2600]
Length:   [150, 550]

The LMM converges if you re-scale your predictors.  I would suggest:

E12L$cExp = E12L$cExp - mean(E12L$cExp)
E12L$cDuration = (E12L$Duration - mean(E12L$Duration)) / 1600
E12L$cLength = (E12L$Length - mean(E12L$Length)) / 400

-Dale Barr

