On 07/07/15 15:48, Goldberg, Ariel M wrote:
> Would you mind explaining how you came up with the values for the
> denominators? Is there a general rule of thumb?

I simply centered the variables and divided through by the range 
(maximum minus minimum); the transformed variables will all have a range 
of [-.5, .5].  For this particular study, dividing through by the range 
makes more sense than using z-scores, because the levels of the variable 
were not sampled; they were defined by the experimental design.

