Hi Roger,
I've been using markdown / Rmarkdown a fair amount in the last year or two
(e.g., for the [phonR vignette][http://drammock.github.io/phonR/] and for a
couple articles).  My impressions:

- I really like the "readable source" aspect of markdown vs. LaTeX
- For webpages I find Rmarkdown + knitr to work really well, though I've
noticed some quirks running it through the RStudio GUI so I prefer to have
a build script or makefile run through bash.
- For PDF output, I've had best results converting the Rmarkdown to a plain
markdown (via knitr), converting the markdown to LaTeX source using pandoc
(and a custom LaTeX template) and then compiling using (Xe)LaTeX. LaTeX can
be mixed in with the Rmarkdown source as needed (e.g., for equations).

-- dan

